<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Coerced SMB Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Coerced SMB Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">An exploit or test procedure that forces a server to authenticating via SMB protocol under unexpected or manipulated circumstances to evaluate authentication weaknesses.&lt;SEP&gt;An technique that exploits authentication mechanisms over SMB shares exploiting a Boolean response difference to gain unauthorized access.&lt;SEP&gt;An exploitation method that uses manipulated inputs in the reachable login workflow to force SMB authentication attempts.&lt;SEP&gt;An authentication bypass attack that forces a system to authenticate via SMB using controlled inputs, leading to potential privilege escalation or lateral movement.&lt;SEP&gt;Technique using SMB protocol to force authentication attempts against target systems with reusable credential data.&lt;SEP&gt;An exploitation technique forcing an SMB share to authenticate with stolen or guessed credentials to access resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-000</data>
