<node id="WinRM Credential Login">
  <data key="d0">WinRM Credential Login</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">WinRM Credential Login refers to a technique used to authenticate to Windows Remote Management (WinRM) services by transmitting credentials during the handshake process. This methodology is employed to gain initial access to target endpoints, often followed by further command execution or privilege escalation activities. By leveraging either valid, harvested, or guessed credentials, adversaries can establish sessions and interact with the system remotely. This approach is utilized in both penetration testing and malicious exploitation scenarios to bypass authentication mechanisms and obtain command shell access on Windows-based systems.&lt;SEP&gt;An authentication technique that injects valid credentials during WinRM communications to test privilege escalation or lateral movement.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique using Windows Remote Management to authenticate over HTTP(S) with misconfigured credential checks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e3971755d02df1ca9d73a71e46dde1d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e3971755d02df1ca9d73a71e46dde1d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">barbhack-2025-ctf-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-darkzero-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-eighteen-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-job-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-jobtwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-logging-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-signed-methodology.md</data>
