<node id="Login Workflow">
  <data key="d0">Login Workflow</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Login Workflow refers to a reachable user login and authentication procedure that enables credential submission, session establishment, and access to authenticated functionality. It encompasses the web login interface or process necessary for authentication attacks to proceed, serving as the target condition required by an attacker to manipulate the system. This mechanism includes the flow through which users establish sessions, whether via interactive login or automated processes, ultimately granting access to protected resources and state after successful verification. It also represents a testable component of the system where the login process's reachability and full authentication flow are confirmed.&lt;SEP&gt;A valid and reachable login interface process where user credentials are accepted and sessions are created.&lt;SEP&gt;The complete web-based login process and authentication mechanism exposed to testers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e3971755d02df1ca9d73a71e46dde1d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-000</data>
