</node>
<node id="API Endpoint">
  <data key="d0">API Endpoint</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">API Endpoint: An application programming interface endpoint refers to a network address, commonly via HTTP or HTTPS, that enables remote access to an application's data or functionality. These exposed service points accept input parameters and headers to perform specific actions or return requested data upon authorization or authentication checks. API endpoints serve as the accessible URLs within an application infrastructure, facilitating interaction between different software systems. While they can be publicly or privately reachable, their accessibility often makes them targets for probing or abuse, necessitating robust security measures to ensure controlled and authorized communication.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e3971755d02df1ca9d73a71e46dde1d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">barbhack-2025-ctf-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-barrier-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-guardian-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-logging-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-monitorsfour-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-principal-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785757726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Executable Upload Webshell">
  <data key="d0">Executable Upload Webshell</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">Executable Upload Webshell refers to a cyberattack technique that exploits insufficient input validation in file upload mechanisms of web servers. Attackers upload a malicious payload, which typically takes the form of scripts or binaries, to a writable location that remains accessible via web requests. This successful deployment allows the adversary to achieve unauthorized remote code execution, effectively granting them the capability to issue system commands as authenticated users. Such a compromise establishes persistent remote access to the server, enabling further malicious activities including privilege escalation, lateral movement, and data exfiltration. Commonly, this attack involves uploading malicious scripts—sometimes disguised as benign files such as images—to locations facilitating their execution, often utilizing path traversal vulnerabilities to ensure persistence. By planting web shells that remain accessible via web requests, adversaries maintain ongoing control over the compromised host.&lt;SEP&gt;An action involving uploading and initiating a web shell to grant attacker code execution on the server.&lt;SEP&gt;Technique that uploads malicious web scripts and executes them through a web server component with upload or writable path access.&lt;SEP&gt;A method of submitting and saving malicious scripts or binary executables into a web application so they can be remotely invoked later.&lt;SEP&gt;Reusable malicious input structured to bypass upload restrictions and allow placing arbitrary code for remote execution.&lt;SEP&gt;An action uploading malicious scripts or binaries to a target system and executing them via an accessible handler.&lt;SEP&gt;An attack technique that uploads executable files through web interfaces to gain persistent, privileged access to a host.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-136da9e7ebc65a69c7a4923c2daacd7b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-39047a18b515fcf5a6bcfa50dda4ee3a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e3971755d02df1ca9d73a71e46dde1d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e3971755d02df1ca9d73a71e46dde1d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-00