<node id="Database Dump">
  <data key="d0">Database Dump</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A concrete file artifact containing a full or partial extracted dump of target database tables and data.&lt;SEP&gt;Acquired dump or extract of the database content containing tables, schema, and stored data.&lt;SEP&gt;Database Dump refers to a complete or partial extract of data from a database table retrieved through file read or similar techniques. It encompasses a complete or partial copy of a database's content, including tables, schema, and potentially sensitive information such as credential hashes, user records, and configuration details. Legitimate database dumps are routinely created as part of backup, recovery, and migration processes, functioning as tools for data preservation and management through authorized mechanisms. Conversely, database dumps can also be illicitly obtained via vulnerabilities such as SQL Injection or improperly secured download links, transforming them into high-risk artifacts during data breaches. In these cases, the dump becomes a valuable asset for unauthorized access or malicious exploitation. Overall, a database dump serves as both a vital component for database administration and a sensitive data reservoir that requires careful handling and protection throughout its lifecycle. The extracted content may reveal sensitive or private information contained within one or more database tables, including the database structure and records that expose such data. It is often represented as a file containing either a copy of data from a target database produced via extraction or an analysis artifact used to identify sensitive data during security incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;Syntactically complete data extraction from a database used to exfiltrate sensitive information.&lt;SEP&gt;A complete extraction of one or more database tables or contents obtained via exploitation.&lt;SEP&gt;Complete or partial backup of database contents, often containing tables, schema, and encoded data that may include sensitive information or plaintext credentials.&lt;SEP&gt;Extracted or copied database file extracted through SQL injection or other data access techniques exposing sensitive records.&lt;SEP&gt;Exported database content containing user records, table structures, or sensitive data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-39047a18b515fcf5a6bcfa50dda4ee3a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2af45459b5392b7945360d1fe34d952c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9756198566adacc24b429de0c91a0beb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6b1a9df875b4f4d10c856b106f068993-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f25479dd4ca15c3238c1385baf2d1e75-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-codetwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-conversor-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-snapped-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-slonik-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-eighteen-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-darkzero-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-sorcery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-wingdata-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-hacknet-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-giveback-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-barrier-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;barbhack-2025-ctf-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-monitorsfour-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-browsed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-signed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-guardian-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-interpreter-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-orion-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-breach-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-overwatch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-bamboo-methodology.md</data>
