<node id="Privilege Escalation Path">
  <data key="d0">Privilege Escalation Path</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-39047a18b515fcf5a6bcfa50dda4ee3a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2af45459b5392b7945360d1fe34d952c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-39047a18b515fcf5a6bcfa50dda4ee3a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-136da9e7ebc65a69c7a4923c2daacd7b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f25479dd4ca15c3238c1385baf2d1e75-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2af45459b5392b7945360d1fe34d952c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6b1a9df875b4f4d10c856b106f068993-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-198b423c5fcf5fd72465af48d35436e5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a267c575fd1175171a41707a2ac80c03-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-abae2141b512784d1f09780ffa398a5d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d2">Provides steps to reach higher permissions by pivoting through systems authenticated by cracked credentials.&lt;SEP&gt;Privilege Escalation Path refers to a reusable sequence of steps, techniques, or conditions that allow an attacker to progress from lower system privileges to higher privileges or full control of a target system. It represents a feasible chain of exploitable weaknesses, misconfigurations, or trusted relationships that together facilitate unauthorized access elevation. Often serving as a pivot point following initial compromise—for example via web shells in Windows Active Directory environments—this pathway underpins broader attacks aimed at achieving domain-wide control or root access. The term describes a strategic objective to increase an attacker's effective permissions beyond their initial constrained role, moving toward administrative or root-level access within the target environment. A Privilege Escalation Path constitutes a sequence of actions, discovered conditions, or interconnected vulnerabilities that permit the systematic accumulation of higher-level system permissions after initial access is obtained. This sequence enables lateral movement, expanded operational ability, and ultimately grants the user permissions more extensive than originally permitted, thereby facilitating unauthorized control. Acquired credentials such as valid user hashes further support this progression by allowing the attacker to authenticate and perform subsequent privilege escalation steps when encountering accounts with higher scopes or admin roles.&lt;SEP&gt;A pre-existing method or sequence of steps the attacker can follow to elevate their permissions from an initial low-privilege context to SYSTEM or root level.&lt;SEP&gt;A sequence of vulnerabilities or permission misconfigurations that can lead to gaining higher administrative privileges.&lt;SEP&gt;A sequence of actions or existing session states that lead toward gaining higher administrative or system access rights.&lt;SEP&gt;A strategic result where an attacker moves up system permissions to gain administrative or root-level access.&lt;SEP&gt;A chain of exploits allowing attacker access to increase permissions to root or admin level.</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackerCapability</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-job-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-codetwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-conversor-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-slonik-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-cctv-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-bruno-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-variatype-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-imagery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-darkzero-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-sorcery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-nanocorp-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-wingdata-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-expressway-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-jobtwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-previous-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-devarea-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-airtouch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;barbhack-2025-ctf-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-monitorsfour-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-facts-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-browsed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-signed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-abducted-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-interpreter-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-principal-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-orion-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-breach-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-overwatch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-bamboo-methodology.md</data>
