<node id="Credential Exposure">
  <data key="d0">Credential Exposure</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">Credential Exposure is a vulnerability class wherein sensitive authentication information—such as login credentials, API keys, session tokens, passwords, or hashes—becomes unintentionally disclosed. This exposure arises due to application misconfigurations, insecure storage mechanisms, or insufficient data sanitization, often manifesting when such data appears in server responses, source code, program logs, or error messages as a result of improper handling, storage, or transmission controls. It is a significant security flaw resulting from inadequate protection surrounding authentication materials and represents an objective target for attackers, who can exploit leaked credentials to gain unauthorized access to user accounts or systems, thereby compromising identity and system integrity. Accordingly, it encompasses weaknesses where user credentials are exposed through application responses, logs, insecure transmission or storage of authentication secrets, or the accidental return of sensitive authentication data—including hashes—by server outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;A flaw where authentication details, tokens, or access credentials are unintentionally readable via source code, files, or verbose responses.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where user credentials or authentication information can be leaked accidentally.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-abae2141b512784d1f09780ffa398a5d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-136da9e7ebc65a69c7a4923c2daacd7b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6b1a9df875b4f4d10c856b106f068993-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6b1a9df875b4f4d10c856b106f068993-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e3971755d02df1ca9d73a71e46dde1d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f25479dd4ca15c3238c1385baf2d1e75-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-abducted-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-airtouch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-breach-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-browsed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-bruno-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-conversor-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-darkzero-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-devarea-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-eighteen-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-facts-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-gavel-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-guardian-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-hacknet-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-imagery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-interpreter-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-job-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-jobtwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-logging-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-nanocorp-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-orion-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-previous-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-principal-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-sorcery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-soulmate-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-wingdata-methodology.md</data>
