<node id="Command Injection">
  <data key="d0">Command Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">Command Injection is a vulnerability class wherein malicious commands are executed on a target system by tricking an application into running user-controlled input as valid system commands. This weakness arises when an application directly incorporates external input into a system call or API without adequate sanitization or validation. Consequently, an attacker can inject arbitrary system shell commands into input fields or parameters, such as web forms, API requests, or scripts. Once executed, these injected commands run with the privileges of the vulnerable application, potentially granting the attacker unauthorized access, modification of system data, or full control over the host operating system. Essentially, Command Injection exploits improper handling of user input to enable the execution of arbitrary system commands on the server, representing a severe threat to application and system security.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-abae2141b512784d1f09780ffa398a5d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-198b423c5fcf5fd72465af48d35436e5-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-abducted-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-airtouch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-browsed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-conversor-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-devarea-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-gavel-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-guardian-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-imagery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-monitorsfour-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-soulmate-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-variatype-methodology.md</data>
