<node id="Config File">
  <data key="d0">Config File</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-39047a18b515fcf5a6bcfa50dda4ee3a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2af45459b5392b7945360d1fe34d952c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a267c575fd1175171a41707a2ac80c03-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-abae2141b512784d1f09780ffa398a5d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f25479dd4ca15c3238c1385baf2d1e75-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d2">A concrete configuration file artifact that often contains environment variables, server settings, or application secrets.&lt;SEP&gt;Config File refers to a file containing configuration data that defines system or application settings. It commonly includes sensitive information such as API credentials, database connection strings, environmental variables, passwords, and service credentials. These files often serve to specify runtime parameters or delivery configurations and are frequently readable or mutable. Due to the presence of such sensitive data, configuration files are a prime target during cybersecurity reconnaissance as potential sources of exploitable information. They appear in various formats including `.env` and `.ini` and may reveal file paths, database connections, or API endpoints essential to an adversary. Configuration files extracted from target systems notably expose structures like hardcoded secrets, internal network details, and access controls. In essence, they encapsulate configuration data that, if compromised, provides attackers significant insight into system architecture, credentials, and sensitive operational parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;A system or application configuration file extracted during an attack that may contain secrets or service details.&lt;SEP&gt;System or application configuration data file containing secrets, connection strings, or system settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Configuration files (e.g., JSON, properties, environment configs) extracted from systems to expose secrets, endpoints, or tuning details.&lt;SEP&gt;Configuration files grabbed from writable paths, exposed repositories or application directories containing secrets, connection strings or access tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;A system or application configuration file containing sensitive settings or credentials.</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
