<node id="URL Userinfo Confusion Payload">
  <data key="d0">URL Userinfo Confusion Payload</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-abae2141b512784d1f09780ffa398a5d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-39047a18b515fcf5a6bcfa50dda4ee3a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a267c575fd1175171a41707a2ac80c03-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6b1a9df875b4f4d10c856b106f068993-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2af45459b5392b7945360d1fe34d952c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d2">URL Userinfo Confusion Payload is a reusable, parameterized malicious input technique designed to exploit variations in URL userinfo encoding to bypass access controls, authentication mechanisms, or filtering logic. It takes the form of a malformed or ambiguous string embedded within URL path or query components, intentionally confusing the parsing of hostname/userinfo segments. By probing defenses against misinterpreted userinfo parameters, this technique exploits inconsistencies in URL handler implementations to evade authorization checks, proxy filters, or authentication validation. Common targets include userinfo and query parameters, crafted with ambiguous syntax to disrupt strict adherence to URL structure interpretation. Functionally, it serves both as a malicious input probe to circumvent security mechanisms and as a vehicle for testing bypass techniques such as path traversal, directory listing circumvention, or injecting unauthorized parameters through URL encoding manipulation or parameter injection ambiguities. Ultimately, it is a malformed URL parameter or parameter injection pattern leveraging userinfo syntax variations to confuse server-side user info resolution and authentication validation, often aiming to expose authenticated session tokens, trick authentication flows, or exploit gaps in input sanitization and URL routing logic.&lt;SEP&gt;Reusable parameterized malicious input designed to confuse or bypass URL authentication mechanisms by manipulating userinfo components in the request path.&lt;SEP&gt;A parameter substitution pattern that misconfigured applications treat as path information rather than authentication data.&lt;SEP&gt;A reusable malicious input pattern that manipulates URL userinfo to confuse server-side authorization logic.&lt;SEP&gt;A parameterized or modified URL userinfo segment designed to confuse or bypass input validation mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
