<node id="Server-Side URL Fetch Feature">
  <data key="d0">Server-Side URL Fetch Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Server-Side URL Fetch Feature is a server capability that allows backend code to send outbound HTTP or HTTPS requests to external or internal endpoints based on user input, application logic, or other dynamic components. It enables the dynamic loading of resources and facilitates flexible integration with other systems by allowing URLs to be specified dynamically rather than hard-coded. However, this feature presents significant security risks, including the potential for Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) attacks if input is not properly sanitized or validated. Consequently, server-side URL fetch implementations must incorporate robust input validation and strict access controls to mitigate these threats while preserving the utility of the feature for legitimate backend services and dynamic content retrieval. The capability is realized through server components configured to perform URL fetching or redirects when dynamic parameters are provided, and encompasses functions that use external URL API calls to process input before returning a response or rendering dynamic content.&lt;SEP&gt;A target capability to make outbound HTTP(S) requests from the server side.&lt;SEP&gt;A server mechanism where user-controlled input is passed into an HTTP or URL-fetching function.&lt;SEP&gt;A server-side capability to dynamically fetch external or internal URLs based on user-supplied paths or parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Server capability to perform outbound HTTP(S) requests triggered by user input or application logic.&lt;SEP&gt;A target functionality that performs server-side HTTP requests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-39047a18b515fcf5a6bcfa50dda4ee3a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6b1a9df875b4f4d10c856b106f068993-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e3971755d02df1ca9d73a71e46dde1d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-00