<node id="Verbose Error Disclosure">
  <data key="d0">Verbose Error Disclosure</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Verbose Error Disclosure describes a software behavior where applications or servers return overly detailed error responses to the client. This information typically includes sensitive backend data such as file paths, function names, variable names, stack traces, server types, database schema details, or specific SQL syntax. The disclosure frequently occurs when the system processes invalid or malformed input but fails to apply security filtering, allowing internal implementation specifics—intended only for developers—to become visible to unauthorized users. By revealing private data including system configuration and application logic, verbose error disclosure can expose the underlying system architecture, creating vulnerabilities that may be exploited in further attacks or reverse engineering efforts. This phenomenon functions as an observable signal indicating potential misconfigurations in error handling that compromise application security and internal data privacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9756198566adacc24b429de0c91a0beb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-001</data>
