</node>
<node id="Uploaded Files Are Web Served">
  <data key="d0">Uploaded Files Are Web Served</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Target configuration that serves user-uploaded content when requested via direct file path or browser-based URI.&lt;SEP&gt;A target behavior or condition where files uploaded through an upload handler are ultimately served or executed by the web server via a public URL.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where files uploaded by users are served as web content when requested.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where uploaded files are publicly or attacker-accessible via HTTP.&lt;SEP&gt;Files uploaded by users are directly accessible via URL paths without proper access restrictions or signature verification.&lt;SEP&gt;A target condition where uploaded files are served by the web server after upload, creating an avenue for malicious content delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-airtouch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-breach-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-browsed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-conversor-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-gavel-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-imagery-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785756575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
