<node id="Apache">
  <data key="d0">Apache</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">Apache is an open-source web server software package installed on a host to deliver web content and manage web applications. It serves HTTP requests by processing and delivering web pages to browsers, commonly supporting dynamic content handling and integration with authentication modules. As a widely deployed server software, it is frequently involved in web application serving and is often documented within attack methodologies due to its prevalence in target environments where security testing and exploit scenarios are executed. Available in multiple configurations, Apache typically functions as either a standalone server or as part of a proxy setup, routing requests to upstream application logic to power hosted web services including dynamic web applications and PHP-driven sites.&lt;SEP&gt;A web server software handling HTTP requests before passing them to application logic.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f25479dd4ca15c3238c1385baf2d1e75-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-airtouch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-barrier-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-conversor-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-devarea-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-interpreter-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-nanocorp-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-wingdata-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785758202</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Container">
  <data key="d0">Container</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">A runtime environment that packages applications and their dependencies, often deployed on Linux hosts.&lt;SEP&gt;Container is a software containerization environment that encapsulates applications, dependencies, and runtime configurations. It represents a lightweight operating system-level virtualization method that packages applications and their necessary components for deployment and isolation. Containerization platforms, such as those commonly used in orchestration environments, allow applications to run isolated from the host system while sharing the host kernel. These environments are utilized across various deployment strategies, including isolation of web application components and the operation of containerized applications. In incident response and security contexts, containerized environments may also be subject to attacks, such as web shell uploads, which exploit these isolated yet network-accessible containers for unauthorized code execution. Overall, containers provide a standardized means to package, deploy, and run applications consistently across different computing environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Isolation environment for deploying applications potentially introducing container escape or misconfiguration risks.&lt;SEP&gt;A runtime environment that packages applications and their dependencies into isolated units.&lt;SEP&gt;A pedantized deployment unit (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes) with potential container escape vectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Containerized deployment environment used to host the application components&lt;SEP&gt;A virtualized compute environment for isolated application deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-airtouch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-conversor-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-nanocorp-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-barrier-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-eighteen-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-monitorsfour-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-facts-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-breach-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-darkzero-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-browsed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-interpreter-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-principal-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785757700</data>
