</node>
<node id="Client-Side Authorization">
  <data key="d0">Client-Side Authorization</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">Client-Side Authorization is a weakness class where authorization checks occur solely on the client side, rendering them susceptible to bypass by manipulating front-end code, input parameters, session tokens, or authorization headers. This vulnerability arises because authorization decisions, such as permissions and access control, are based on data provided by the client application rather than being enforced by backend server logic. As a result, any client-side validation or session management mechanisms cannot be reliably trusted, as they can be easily overridden or circumvented before reaching the server for verification. This design flaw leaves applications exposed to various attacks, including unauthorized access, privilege escalation, and cross-site scripting exploits, given the inherent trust in client-provided information absent robust server-side validation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-airtouch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-barrier-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-breach-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-facts-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-gavel-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-guardian-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-principal-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-sorcery-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785758009</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Path Traversal">
  <data key="d0">Path Traversal</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">Path Traversal is a cybersecurity weakness wherein an attacker exploits specially-crafted input containing directory traversal sequences—most commonly the `../` pattern—to access files, directories, or resources located outside the intended directory structure or web root. This vulnerability occurs when user-supplied path components are not adequately sanitized, thereby allowing the attacker to bypass access controls and navigate the file system beyond authorized boundaries. By injecting relative path traversal sequences such as `../../` into input used to construct file paths, an attacker can attempt unauthorized reads, writes, or execution of sensitive or critical resources outside their intended scope. At its core, this issue stems from insufficient validation of user input during file path construction, which may lead to the exposure of confidential data or full system compromise. This vulnerability often permits access to any arbitrary directories or files on the target filesystem, enabling breaches through manipulation of path references with special characters or traversal sequences that exceed the permitted web root.&lt;SEP&gt;An input handling weakness where directory navigation characters bypass intended path restrictions.&lt;SEP&gt;Attack surface allowing directory traversal references (e.g., `../../../`) to access files or resources outside intended directories.&lt;SEP&gt;A flaw where user-controlled input is improperly used in file system paths to access unauthorized files or directories.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness class enabling an attacker to access files or directories outside the intended web root by manipulating URL or input paths.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness in file system handling that allows access to files outside the intended directory.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-136da9e7ebc65a69c7a4923c2daacd7b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6b1a9df875b4f4d10c856b106f068993-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2af45459b5392b7945360d1fe34d952c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-198b423c5fcf5fd72465af48d35436e5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-198b423c5fcf5fd72465af48d35436e5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f25479dd4ca15c3238c1385baf2d1e75-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-airtouch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-conversor-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-gavel-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-hacknet-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-eighteen-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-bruno-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-facts-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-breach-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-darkzero-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-browsed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-bamboo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-guardian-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-imagery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-job-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-jobtwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-previous-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-principal-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-slonik-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-sorcery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-soulmate-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-variatype-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-wingdata-methodology.md</data>
