<node id="Localhost-Only Service Exists">
  <data key="d0">Localhost-Only Service Exists</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6b1a9df875b4f4d10c856b106f068993-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-39047a18b515fcf5a6bcfa50dda4ee3a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2af45459b5392b7945360d1fe34d952c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-198b423c5fcf5fd72465af48d35436e5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9756198566adacc24b429de0c91a0beb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f25479dd4ca15c3238c1385baf2d1e75-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d2">The technique is applicable only when an internal service bound to localhost is exposed via an SSRF vector.&lt;SEP&gt;Localhost-Only Service Exists refers to an internal service strictly bound to loopback network interfaces such as `127.0.0.1` or `::1`, intended to isolate system functionality from direct external network access. Because these services are restricted to being reachable only from processes running on the same host, they are commonly deployed to support internal system operations without broad internet exposure. Despite this intended logical isolation, such configurations frequently present attack surfaces that can be exploited via Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF). Attackers can bypass the localhost restriction by abusing other network interfaces, APIs, or misconfigurations to compromise the service from outside the host. Consequently, a localhost-bound service remains a potential vulnerability whenever it can be accessed by an attacker through indirect means, even if external networks cannot directly reach it. The security of these services therefore depends heavily on stringent controls that prevent unintended or malicious external interaction, as the localhost binding alone does not offer sufficient protection against sophisticated bypass techniques.</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-snapped-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-slonik-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-eighteen-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-cctv-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-imagery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-darkzero-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-sorcery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-nanocorp-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-wingdata-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-giveback-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-hacknet-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-jobtwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-devarea-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-airtouch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-gavel-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-barrier-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-monitorsfour-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-facts-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-browsed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-signed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-guardian-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-interpreter-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-orion-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-soulmate-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-overwatch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-bamboo-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785757825</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reachable Admin Panel">
  <data key="d0">Reachable Admin Panel</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Reachable Admin Panel refers to an administrative interface or dashboard that is accessible within the application's attack surface. It functions as a web interface that grants administrative privileges and can be exploited as a pivot point during an attack. This panel represents an administrative interface or management area that is accessible over the network, providing privileged functionality to any external observer able to reach it. Essentially, it is a target condition in which administrative interface endpoints or management consoles are reachable and exposed, allowing an attacker to attempt authentication and gain unauthorized control.&lt;SEP&gt;A hidden or discoverable administrative interface available for testing.&lt;SEP&gt;A web interface or management console restricted to administrative accounts, serving as a target for authentication and privilege testing.&lt;SEP&gt;An administrative interface that handles user-controlled input and is reachable for testing.&lt;SEP&gt;An exposed administrative interface reachable during reconnaissance that opens further privilege and configuration access.&lt;SEP&gt;A target administrative interface or dashboard that is accessible via internal network routes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9756198566adacc24b429de0c91a0beb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9756198566adacc24b429de0c91a0beb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-bamboo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-codetwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-eighteen-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-facts-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-gavel-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-giveback-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-imagery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-nanocorp-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-snapped-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-sorcery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-soulmate-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785758054</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Source Review Access">
  <data key="d0">Source Review Access</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackerCapability</data>
  <data key="d2">Possession of found password hashes enables the attacker to perform further reconnaissance, such as getting full account details from account recovery or lookup functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Attacker ability to access and download the source code, configuration files, or build artifacts from exposed repositories.&lt;SEP&gt;An attacker capability to access and examine source code or technical documentation of the target system.&lt;SEP&gt;The attacker can retrieve and analyze source code from exposed repositories such as Git.&lt;SEP&gt;A capability providing the ability to view and analyze source code or configuration files to identify further weaknesses.&lt;SEP&gt;Permission to view or extract accessible source code from repositories or download points.&lt;SEP&gt;The ability to access and inspect application source code, configuration files, or repository history to discover vulnerabilities or extract secrets before acting on them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-conversor-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-jobtwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-monitorsfour-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-imagery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-darkzero-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-bamboo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-signed-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785757810</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authenticated Session">
  <data key="d0">Authenticated Session</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Requires valid session tokens but access often grants authenticated context where further actions require session integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Authenticated Session is an active user login session on a target system, established with valid credentials that have been verified as legitimate. Such a session maintains continuity and provides the necessary context to request and access restricted resources, systems, or functionalities that would otherwise be unavailable to un-authenticated users. In cybersecurity contexts, this authenticated state is often sought by attackers to conduct post-exploitation maneuvers, extend their foothold, or escalate privileges by abusing the legitimate identity or access permissions associated with the session. Typically manifested as session tokens, stored state, or an active user context, an authenticated session grants permission to interact with system resources under the assumed identity of the verified user, making it a critical element in both normal system operation and malicious activities such as lateral movement and privilege abuse.&lt;SEP&gt;Active session with valid authentications that already authenticated and can be leveraged for further requests.&lt;SEP&gt;An established session with valid user credentials providing access to protected features.&lt;SEP&gt;The attacker already possesses a valid session cookie or token proving user credentials&lt;SEP&gt;Presence of a valid user session token that can impersonate the user for API or web requests.&lt;SEP&gt;An active session with valid user or service authentication credentials that maintains session state across requests for continued exploitation.&lt;SEP&gt;An active session token or HTTP cookie that maintains state for an already-authenticated user.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-39047a18b515fcf5a6bcfa50dda4ee3a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-39047a18b515fcf5a6bcfa50dda4ee3a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-136da9e7ebc65a69c7a4923c2daacd7b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-job-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-codetwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-giveback-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-cctv-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-bruno-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-monitorsfour-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-principal-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-soulmate-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-signed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-bamboo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-devarea-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785757825</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Source Code">
  <data key="d0">Source Code</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Source Code refers to the actual programming files constituting a software project, serving as the foundational composition of the application. These files contain application logic, sensitive configurations, hidden credentials such as hard-coded secrets and API endpoints, database schemas, authentication mechanisms, and reusable components. They are often extracted from exposed or copied repositories, obtained through repository access, or discovered via file system read techniques. From a security perspective, the source code acts as a critical target for analysis, where reviewing its contents reveals potential vulnerabilities, misconfigurations, or logical flaws that may compromise system integrity or enable privilege escalation. Accordingly, Source Code encompasses concrete source files, entire application codebases, or specific extracted segments obtained through reconnaissance or reverse engineering, with the common purpose of exposing implementation details necessary for identifying security weaknesses or facilitating further exploitation.&lt;SEP&gt;Concrete files containing application source code that may be disclosed, reviewed, or manipulated during an attack timeline.&lt;SEP&gt;Complete application source files compiled or interpreted by the target environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Complete source code files or repositories obtained through review or disclosure that reveal internal logic and credentials.&lt;SEP&gt;Direct codebase files leaked or accessible through source code review or exposed repository, often containing hardcoded credentials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-bamboo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-barrier-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-browsed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-codetwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-conversor-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-darkzero-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-eighteen-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-giveback-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-guardian-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-monitorsfour-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-nanocorp-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-orion-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-previous-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-sorcery-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785758007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uploaded Path Disclosure">
  <data key="d0">Uploaded Path Disclosure</data>
  <data key="d1">ObservableSignal</data>
  <data key="d2">Server response that includes the full local filesystem path of an uploaded file, indicating inadequate input validation on file handling.&lt;SEP&gt;Disclosure of internal paths or file locations via an upload interface.&lt;SEP&gt;Disclosure of local file paths or structures in server responses after a file upload is processed or parsed.&lt;SEP&gt;A server response that reveals the local file path or directory structure based on how user input is handed to the file system&lt;SEP&gt;Server response that reveals the internal filepath used upon upload.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f25479dd4ca15c3238c1385baf2d1e75-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-bamboo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-breach-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-principal-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-wingdata-methodology.md</data>
