<node id="NGINX">
  <data key="d0">NGINX</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">NGINX is a widely-used, high-performance web server and reverse proxy software. It excels at managing HTTP traffic by routing client requests to appropriate backend services and can be configured with virtual hosts and other features to tailor web traffic handling. In practice, it often serves as an intermediary, parsing and filtering incoming requests before passing them on to backend applications, and it is also commonly utilized to handle load balancing. This capability makes NGINX a core component in many web infrastructures, frequently employed for hosting API endpoints and securing server-side URL fetching operations within web applications. Moreover, its widespread adoption has made it a frequent target for activities such as virtual host discovery in security assessments and an example of proxy misconfigurations.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-performance web server or reverse proxy software commonly used as a web server gateway.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6b1a9df875b4f4d10c856b106f068993-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-barrier-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-hacknet-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-orion-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-facts-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-imagery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-browsed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-soulmate-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785758052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MySQL">
  <data key="d0">MySQL</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">MySQL is a freely available open-source relational database management system widely used for data storage and retrieval in web applications. It is a common component in web application stacks, frequently paired with PHP. Due to its widespread deployment, MySQL is a frequent target in cybersecurity threats, particularly SQL injection attacks, where adversaries attempt to extract, manipulate, or compromise sensitive data. Consequently, it occupies a notable place within the context of application security, with its credentials and stored information being vulnerable to exploitation through injection techniques.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6b1a9df875b4f4d10c856b106f068993-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f25479dd4ca15c3238c1385baf2d1e75-chunk-000</data>
