<node id="Accessible SMB Share">
  <data key="d0">Accessible SMB Share</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">An accessible network share reachable by the attacker used for authentication and lateral movement.&lt;SEP&gt;A shared folder on a server that is reachable through SMB protocol without proper access control.&lt;SEP&gt;A shared directory accessible over the SMB protocol for credential prompting or file transfer.&lt;SEP&gt;A shared folder exposed over SMB/Windows networking interfaces reachable to the tester.&lt;SEP&gt;SMB share reachable over the network from the attacker.&lt;SEP&gt;A shared SMB resource reachable over the network that may lack proper authentication or authorization checks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-136da9e7ebc65a69c7a4923c2daacd7b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-000</data>
