<node id="Coerced Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Coerced Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness where application logic accepts malformed or alternative authentication mechanisms that bypass normal login controls.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where the system can be tricked into authenticating with unintended credentials during data injection or special character manipulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Weakness allowing an attacker to force the server to authenticate using credentials embedded in crafted input or file paths.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-001</data>
