<node id="Server-Side Request Forgery">
  <data key="d0">Server-Side Request Forgery</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness class in which the server makes unauthorized outbound requests using attacker-controlled parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;An attack technique where an application is induced to make requests to remote or internal backend services.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where server-side components fetch remote URLs specified by the user, allowing attacker-controlled requests to internal or external systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where the server performs unexpected outbound requests to attacker-controlled or trusted IP addresses based on user input.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-000</data>
