<node id="Deserialization Gadget Execution">
  <data key="d0">Deserialization Gadget Execution</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6b1a9df875b4f4d10c856b106f068993-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d2">The API may validate deserialized claims as part of token processing during authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing action that exploits insecure object deserialization to achieve an escalation goal.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique that exploits unsafe deserialization of arbitrary data to invoke existing or custom object-gadget chains leading to code execution.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing or attacking action that leverages deserialization vulnerabilities to execute malicious code or access internal objects.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique to trigger undetected execution of code within deserialized objects through crafted payloads.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique that invokes vulnerable deserialization handlers with crafted payloads to achieve unauthorized code execution.&lt;SEP&gt;Technique exploiting unsafe deserialization of external objects to trigger gadget chains or untrusted code execution.</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-codetwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-gavel-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-hacknet-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-interpreter-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-sorcery-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785758007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SQL Injection">
  <data key="d0">SQL Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">Weakness where user input is directly included into SQL queries allowing unauthorized data access, modification or execution.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where user input is unintentionally included in SQL queries, allowing database manipulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Insertion of malicious SQL statements into user inputs to manipulate database queries for unauthorized data extraction or command execution.&lt;SEP&gt;A logic flaw in input handling allowing injection of arbitrary SQL statements for data manipulation or access.&lt;SEP&gt;A broad class of web application vulnerabilities where user input is improperly validated as part of an SQL query.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-198b423c5fcf5fd72465af48d35436e5-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-conversor-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-gavel-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-imagery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-monitorsfour-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-variatype-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785758135</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)">
  <data key="d0">Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">An attack that forces a server to make unintended requests to internal or external resources controlled by the attacker.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique exploiting server functions to make unintended requests to internal or external services via the server as an intermediary.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-devarea-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-sorcery-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785758010</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft IIS Upload Handler">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft IIS Upload Handler</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific type of web server component associated with Microsoft Internet Information Services (IIS) that processes file upload submissions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-devarea-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785755642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
