<node id="Wildcard Command Filter Bypass Payload">
  <data key="d0">Wildcard Command Filter Bypass Payload</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">Input string designed to bypass wildcard-based command filtering by tricking partial matches.&lt;SEP&gt;A reusable payload pattern containing wildcards to evade input validation filters in database or shell contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;A command or input string using wildcards to bypass shell or command execution filters by circumventing input pattern matching.&lt;SEP&gt;Parameterized command injection input that uses wildcards to evade filter patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Reusable parameterized malicious input designed to evade server-side wildcard command filters used by local service discovery probes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-001</data>
