<node id="Egress Firewall">
  <data key="d0">Egress Firewall</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">A security device that monitors and restricts outbound network traffic based on defined policies.&lt;SEP&gt;A network boundary control that monitors and blocks outgoing traffic from the target environment.&lt;SEP&gt;A network security device or configuration that blocks unauthorized outbound traffic, often used to restrict data exfiltration.&lt;SEP&gt;Network boundary protection designed to restrict outbound connections from within the perimeter to the external network.&lt;SEP&gt;A network security device enforcing outbound traffic policies that restrict external communication from internal hosts to limit lateral movement or external service probing.&lt;SEP&gt;A component that controls outbound network traffic from inside the network to external networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a267c575fd1175171a41707a2ac80c03-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-expressway-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-nanocorp-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-overwatch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-signed-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785757809</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Name-Based Virtual Host Routing">
  <data key="d0">Name-Based Virtual Host Routing</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Name-Based Virtual Host Routing is a web server configuration capability, commonly implemented in servers such as Apache and Nginx, which allows multiple domains to be hosted on a single IP address. It functions by utilizing the HTTP Host header value contained within incoming requests to determine which virtual host configuration should handle the request. This setup enables the mapping of virtual hostnames to distinct application directories based solely on this header, facilitating the sharing of a single IP address among multiple hostnames while ensuring proper routing to the respective web applications associated with each hostname.&lt;SEP&gt;Hostname resolution behavior where multiple domains or subdomains map to the same server based on HTTP/HTTPS Host headers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6b1a9df875b4f4d10c856b106f068993-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9756198566adacc24b429de0c91a0beb-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-facts-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-giveback-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-hacknet-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-orion-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-overwatch-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-previous-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-snapped-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785757923</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual Host Discovery">
  <data key="d0">Virtual Host Discovery</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9756198566adacc24b429de0c91a0beb-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d2">The discovery technique utilizes virtual host functionality to probe for backend resources.&lt;SEP&gt;A reconnaissance method to identify and enumerate virtual hosts bound to a target server based on user-controlled or arbitrary DNS/URL inputs.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique utilizing name-based virtual host routing to discover hostnames associated with the target domain.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing action to identify virtual host configurations, enabling further service enumeration and manipulation.&lt;SEP&gt;An action identifying backend virtual hosts by fuzzing hostnames in the request.</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d4">htb-facts-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-giveback-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-previous-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785757701</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual Host Name">
  <data key="d0">Virtual Host Name</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A concrete artifact identifying the hostname configured as a target for name-based virtual hosting in web infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific hostname used for HTTP virtual hosting configuration that identifies a web server's host environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The configured hostname used in name-based virtual host routing discovered during reconnaissance.&lt;SEP&gt;A discovered hostname parameterized within an HTTP Host header used for application routing.&lt;SEP&gt;A hostname discovered through virtual host enumeration identifying internal backend services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000</data>
