  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness where user input is unsanitized and interpreted as a path to filesystem resources, enabling unauthorized access to sensitive files.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where user-controlled path is included by the server without sanitization.&lt;SEP&gt;An action exploiting a path traversal vulnerability to read or include local files.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness class in web applications where user input is used unsafely in file operation functions.</data>
