  <data key="d2">A concrete file artifact storing user login information such as usernames and plaintext or hashed passwords.&lt;SEP&gt;Compromised or replicated user credentials (username and/or passwords) extracted from the target environment.&lt;SEP&gt;A concrete artifact consisting of username/password pairs, access keys, or other identity data that provides authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;The successful forgery often results in possession of data that behaves like valid user credentials, useful for subsequent privilege escalation.&lt;SEP&gt;Usernames, passwords, or session tokens obtained during an attack, often reusable for further compromise.&lt;SEP&gt;Acquired or stolen credentials can be directly used to authenticate and gain interactive shell access to a compromised system.</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
