<edge source="Boolean Response Difference" target="Offline Password Cracking">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Boolean Response Difference in Offline Password Cracking refers to a technique used to identify valid account guesses during hash cracking without live password verification. This method relies on detecting detectable changes in server responses, often framed as boolean values (such as 'true' for a correct guess and 'false' for an incorrect one), which signal whether a password or username guess aligns with stored credentials. It operates under the precondition that such boolean response differences are available as feedback following each guess. By analyzing these mismatches, the technique sets apart valid credentials from invalid ones, enabling the identification of successful authentication-related fields—like usernames or password hashes—via response variation rather than direct validation. It is commonly employed in credential extraction scenarios where guessing attempts are made offline using precomputed hash databases to validate guesses solely based on the nature of the server’s feedback rather than executing live checks.</data>
  <data key="d9">detects,detects using,detects via,indicates,leverages,produces,requires,utilizes</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9756198566adacc24b429de0c91a0beb-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">htb-breach-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-darkzero-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-facts-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-guardian-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-imagery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-jobtwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-previous-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-snapped-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1785757930</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
