</edge>
<edge source="WinRM Credential Login" target="Move Laterally">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Used by attackers to pivot from an initial foothold to other machines and widen their perimeter.&lt;SEP&gt;WinRM Credential Login enables movement across network resources after initial authentication, allowing an attacker to transition from a compromised host to other machines with authorized access.&lt;SEP&gt;The successful login establishes a foothold enabling further lateral movement across network assets once remote command access is achieved.&lt;SEP&gt;Authenticated sessions enable lateral movement across internal resources or services post-breach.&lt;SEP&gt;Technique aids in lateral movement by authenticating and gaining access to additional AD-integrated hosts.&lt;SEP&gt;The capability aids attackers in expanding access across network resources.</data>
  <data key="d9">supports,supports attack goal</data>
