<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="Shell Access">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Uploads a web shell through a valid-looking upload handler to gain interactive command execution on the server.&lt;SEP&gt;Executable Upload Webshell (Shell Access) is a technique used by attackers to gain interactive command shell access to a target server. By successfully uploading a webshell script to the server, an attacker can execute system commands remotely and often persistently. This capability allows for direct control over the host environment, enabling commands to be run as if from a local terminal. Common outcomes include establishing interactive command-line sessions or granting broader remote command execution abilities. In practice, uploading and executing a webshell represents a primary pathway for attackers to achieve shell access on compromised systems, facilitating further malicious activities on the server.&lt;SEP&gt;The webserver-based shell grants an interactive or persistent access channel to the compromised host.</data>
  <data key="d9">achieves,can establish,can support,enables,establishes,establishes attacker capability,establishes capability,requires</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-198b423c5fcf5fd72465af48d35436e5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">htb-job-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;barbhack-2025-ctf-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-jobtwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-variatype-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-soulmate-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-breach-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-darkzero-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-browsed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-signed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-sorcery-methodology.md</data>
