<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="Privilege Escalation Path">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The web shell serves as an initial step or pivot point that forms part of the attacker’s broader path to achieving higher-level access or domain-wide control within Windows Active Directory environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Executing a webshell creates routes or processes that allow deeper system access.&lt;SEP&gt;The webshell provides a route for the attacker to escalate privileges within the compromised environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The webshell can be used as a foothold to escalate rights further.&lt;SEP&gt;The deployed webshell can be leveraged to escalate privileges beyond initial account limits.</data>
  <data key="d9">can establish attacker capability,establishes,establishes attacker capability,establishes capability</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-002</data>
