<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="Accessible Upload Handler">
  <data key="d7">34.0</data>
  <data key="d8">When the web application provides a directory or endpoint where files can be uploaded for resources such as user avatars or themes.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessible Upload Handler, Executable Upload Webshell is a web security vulnerability wherein an attacker exploits an unprotected, reachable file upload function on a web server to deliver and persist malicious script files, specifically web shells. The attack hinges on the presence of a functional upload endpoint that accepts and processes user-supplied content without stringent validation. By submitting malicious executables through HTTP POST or multipart form submissions to this accessible handler, the attacker uploads a web shell to the server's writable storage. This stored malicious code provides remote command execution capabilities, resulting in the compromise of the server's integrity, confidentiality, and availability. Successful execution of this technique is contingent upon the existence of a publicly reachable upload functionality that does not restrict file types or validate inputs before persisting uploaded content. Key prerequisites include an upload endpoint that accepts executable files or user-supplied artifacts and either saves them to server storage or executes them directly. The upload handler serves as the primary conduit for delivering the web shell payload, effectively granting the attacker unauthorized control over the server to run arbitrary system commands.&lt;SEP&gt;A writable or accessible upload handler allows attackers to place malicious web scripts for remote command execution.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique requires the presence of a writable or upload functionality exposed to attacker-supplied content.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique requires an upload endpoint that does not adequately validate file extensions or content.&lt;SEP&gt;The attack relies on the presence of an unrestricted or weakly protected file upload mechanism to place payloads.</data>
  <data key="d9">Requires,accepts,applicable when,applies when,delivers,depends on,enables,exploits,is applicable when,requires,targets,uses</data>
