<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="Executable Extension Interpreted">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Server processing and execution of the uploaded file with an interpreted extension like `.php` or `.js`.&lt;SEP&gt;Interpreting executable file extensions allows malicious scripts to be uploaded and executed.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique is applicable when file extensions that trigger script execution are accepted and parsed.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique requires the server to have active support for executing uploaded scripts with interpreted extensions.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique depends on a server configuration where uploaded malicious files are interpreted as executable by the web server.&lt;SEP&gt;The server neginating or interpreting an executable extension allows successful upload and execution of a webshell.</data>
