<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="PHP">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The technique often targets PHP-based web servers and web applications where file uploads are frequently misconfigured.&lt;SEP&gt;PHP applications are common targets for upload functionality exploitation and webshell deployment due to loose file parsing or extension checks.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique typically targets PHP-based applications where server-side file execution is enabled.</data>
