<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="Extension Blacklist">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">This attack technique can bypass extension blacklist defenses using alternative extension payloads or wildcard filters.&lt;SEP&gt;If file extensions are blacklisted, attackers may attempt to bypass by using unusual or disguised extensions or encoding.&lt;SEP&gt;Technique may disguise uploaded executables with allowed extensions or multiple-part encoding to circumvent the filter.</data>
