<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="WAF Or Request Filter">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Webshell upload attempts can circumvent web application firewall or request validation filters using specific payload patterns and obfuscation.&lt;SEP&gt;Filters can prevent unusually large binary uploads, known shell patterns, or anomalous behaviors used to distribute web shells.&lt;SEP&gt;May block the upload of webshells if the WAF's rules match known malicious patterns in the request or payload.&lt;SEP&gt;The uploaded payload or request generated by the webshell can evade detection by web application firewalls or request filters.</data>
  <data key="d9">may be bypassed by,may block,may bypass,may mitigate</data>
