<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="Uploaded Webshell">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The successful upload results in the creation of this malicious web shell artifact on the target server.&lt;SEP&gt;Executable Upload Webshell (Uploaded Webshell) is an attack technique whose successful outcome is the placement and retrieval of an uploaded webshell artifact on the target system. The technique involves uploading a malicious script to a server, resulting in a resident artifact that remains stored for future manipulation. This stored web shell enables persistent remote command execution, providing threat actors with enduring control over the compromised server. The core activity culminates in the creation of this artifact, ensuring the malicious script is saved on the target server to facilitate ongoing exploitation.</data>
  <data key="d9">can produce,produces,results in</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-198b423c5fcf5fd72465af48d35436e5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-002</data>
