</edge>
<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="Command Execution">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The ability to run arbitrary commands on the host server is an attack goal this technique supports.&lt;SEP&gt;Successful webshell deployment grants the attacker the ability to run commands.&lt;SEP&gt;The uploaded webshell enables the attacker to run arbitrary commands on the target machine.&lt;SEP&gt;The planted webshell enables running arbitrary commands on the server backend.&lt;SEP&gt;The upload and execution of a webshell grants the attacker the ability to run arbitrary commands on the server.&lt;SEP&gt;The web shell enables the attacker to remotely execute system commands.&lt;SEP&gt;The uploaded shell directly provides the capability to execute system commands.</data>
