<edge source="JWT Token Forgery" target="JWT Secret">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The technique can sometimes indirectly expose or reveal the server's cryptographic signing key if token structure or validation fails revealing internal state.&lt;SEP&gt;The token forgery process may require or reveal the underlying signing secret used to validate JWT tokens, making the secret itself an obtained artifact for future attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Requires access to the secret to generate valid signatures bypassing validations.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique requires the attacker to possess or obtain the JWT signing/verification secret for token manipulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Uses the secret key to forge a valid JWT allowing unauthorized access.&lt;SEP&gt;Successful exploitation can uncover or capture the server's JWT signing secret.&lt;SEP&gt;Forgery may yield access to the application's signing secret.</data>
