<edge source="JWT Token Forgery" target="Credentials">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Credentials, specifically JWT Token Forgery, is a cybersecurity technique aimed at generating legitimate-looking JSON Web Tokens that contain malicious or fabricated data. This methodology targets the credentials or authorization secrets embedded within the token structure to deceive systems into accepting unauthorized access. A successful forgery can result in the extraction or validation of the user's actual credentials contained within the token, enabling the attacker to gain unauthorized access to accounts or backend services. Furthermore, successfully forged tokens can lead to the revelation of user credentials to the attacker, which are then used for malicious purposes, such as impersonating authenticated users for lateral movement, privilege escalation, or other forms of exploitation. Consequently, JWT Token Forgery attempts can extract or create compromised credential payloads for further abuse.</data>
  <data key="d9">can produce artifact,produces,produces artifact,targets</data>
