<edge source="JWT Token Forgery" target="Escalate Privileges">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Escalate Privileges, JWT Token Forgery is a security attack technique involving the creation and exploitation of falsified JSON Web Token (JWT) credentials. Attackers forge these tokens to contain expanded privileges or administrative claims that exceed the legitimate rights of the requesting user's account. By doing so, the attacker can falsely prove they possess higher-level access rights within the application or infrastructure. This manipulation of token claims—such as replacing or augmenting role or scope fields—allows the forged token to facilitate the elevation of access levels, effectively bypassing authorization restrictions. Consequently, the technique serves as a direct pathway to increase existing privileges, grant administrative rights, and ultimately achieve elevated access levels, enabling unauthorized actions beyond the original user's permission set.</data>
  <data key="d9">achieves,can support,can support attack goal,supports,supports attack goal</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-0a5b62addae42b2d3e684b41ed40260e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-002</data>
