<edge source="JWT Token Forgery" target="Accessible API Endpoint">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The technique needs exposed API endpoints that use JWT tokens for authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;An attack technique that manipulates or falsifies JSON Web Tokens used for authentication to bypass authorization checks.&lt;SEP&gt;API endpoints requiring JWT validation are the primary targets for injecting manipulated tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;Trusts the attacker-forged or malformed token when sent to endpoints requiring authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique attempts to forge or modify JSON Web Tokens to bypass API authentication checks.&lt;SEP&gt;Invalid or forged JWTs are submitted to endpoints to gain unauthorized API access.&lt;SEP&gt;The attack is feasible when an unauthenticated or exposed API endpoint exists.</data>
