  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Provides legitimate-looking authentication that can be used to invoke shell or remote execution endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Valid forged tokens may grant direct command execution privileges.&lt;SEP&gt;The attacker capability gained is remote command shell access through the forged bearer token bypassing authentication and authorization mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Techniques allowing attacker to forge tokens are facilitated by existing shell access to fetch signing keys.&lt;SEP&gt;Possession of shell access provides the environment to craft and test forged JWT tokens effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Valid tokens can be used to call endpoints that trigger shell or command execution.&lt;SEP&gt;Forgery can be leveraged to gain direct system command execution access.&lt;SEP&gt;Forges tokens to impersonate users with shell access, leading to remote code execution or lateral movement.</data>
