<edge source="Shell Access" target="SQL Injection File Read">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SQL Injection File Read, Shell Access is a cybersecurity attack vector that leverages SQL injection vulnerabilities to read sensitive data or files from a web server. By abusing the database query functionality, attackers can gain access to system files, configuration details, and other critical data residing on the server. Retrieving these files often provides the necessary information or resources to stage a web shell or reverse shell, which in turn grants the attacker interactive command-line execution on the compromised system. This access is frequently used as a foundational step for subsequent privilege escalation and broader compromise of the server infrastructure. Ultimately, the relation describes a multi-stage attack methodology where file read capabilities secured through SQL injection are exploited to ultimately achieve full interactive shell access to the target environment.</data>
  <data key="d9">can establish,can establish attacker capability,can support,establishes,leverages,supports</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2af45459b5392b7945360d1fe34d952c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-198b423c5fcf5fd72465af48d35436e5-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d11">htb-codetwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-devarea-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-giveback-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-previous-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-slonik-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-sorcery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-variatype-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1785758158</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shell Access" target="Offline Password Cracking">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Valid credentials obtained from cracking can be used to gain interactive shell access.&lt;SEP&gt;Gives access to a shell needed to run cracking tools or manual enumeration.&lt;SEP&gt;The successful cracking of credentials can grant shell access to the compromised system.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique establishes the attacker's capability to achieve interactive command access (shell).</data>
  <data key="d9">establishes,supports</data>
