<edge source="Read Sensitive Data" target="SQL Injection File Read">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Read Sensitive Data, SQL Injection File Read is a database exploitation technique that leverages SQL injection vulnerabilities to extract sensitive information or entire files stored on a target server. Attackers utilize this method by injecting crafted queries into input fields, manipulating the database engine to return data that is unintended or unauthorized. The primary objectives include the retrieval of database tables containing confidential information or the extraction of local files residing on the server — such as configuration files (e.g., .ini, .env, .conf), source code, or other sensitive documents (e.g., .pdf, .docx). By abusing the database read mechanism, this technique can reveal credentials, internal configurations, proprietary data, or other critical assets stored on the system. It is a significant threat to data confidentiality and integrity, often facilitating further post-exploitation activities if sensitive data or system details are successfully exfiltrated.&lt;SEP&gt;This technique aims to achieve the attacker goal of retrieving sensitive data.</data>
  <data key="d9">can support,can support attack goal,supports</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8a71a5db941f76cbd976ed319daa4ce-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b3691250d8034efc538f45153325e82-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2af45459b5392b7945360d1fe34d952c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">htb-codetwo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-conversor-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-imagery-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-browsed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-previous-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-devarea-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-pterodactyl-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-signed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-slonik-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1785757886</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
