<edge source="Escalate Privileges" target="Offline Password Cracking">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Escalate Privileges, Offline Password Cracking is a relation indicating that obtaining higher-privileged credentials through the cracking of password hashes enables an attacker to elevate their access rights within a system. Performing offline password cracking provides the necessary credentials to achieve the objective of privilege escalation. Successfully cracked credentials allow progression from standard user roles to more powerful administrative accounts, such as root or system administrator privileges or database administrator (DBA) roles. The technique involves leveraging access to password hashes to discover valid passwords, which are then used to authenticate as higher-privilege accounts and thereby raise the user’s level of system access. This method directly contributes to an attacker's goal of gaining elevated system privileges and control.</data>
  <data key="d9">can support,supports</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-39047a18b515fcf5a6bcfa50dda4ee3a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a267c575fd1175171a41707a2ac80c03-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2af45459b5392b7945360d1fe34d952c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9756198566adacc24b429de0c91a0beb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f25479dd4ca15c3238c1385baf2d1e75-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">htb-bamboo-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-cctv-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-expressway-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-giveback-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-signed-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-slonik-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-snapped-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;htb-wingdata-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1785758212</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Escalate Privileges" target="Privilege Escalation Path">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A successful escalation path facilitates achieving broader administrative privileges and system control.&lt;SEP&gt;This capability represents the outcome or goal for the sequence of privilege escalation steps.&lt;SEP&gt;Describes the attacker goal realized through the ability to increase access.</data>
  <data key="d9">achieves,leads to</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-001</data>
