<edge source="Password Hash" target="Offline Password Cracking">
  <data key="d7">11.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The technique uses captured password hashes as input to recover plaintext credentials and achieve credential exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;Offline Password Cracking, Password Hash is an attack method that leverages brute force or dictionary techniques to extract plaintext passwords from obtained hash artifacts. It utilizes captured password hashes as input for dedicated cracking algorithms, aiming to successfully match or decrypt them to reveal the original plaintext credentials. The technique operates on the principle of reversing the one-way hashing function used during password storage, allowing attackers to systematically guess or attempt common passwords until a match is found. If successful, this process results in the recovery of plaintext passwords from the supplied hash files, thereby exposing sensitive user credentials. Offline password cracking focuses specifically on the brute-force decryption of these leaked or extracted hash artifacts, making it a substantial threat to the security of stored credentials if proper password hashing and salting are not implemented.&lt;SEP&gt;Uses the extracted hash artifact as input for cracking attempts to reveal plaintext passwords.&lt;SEP&gt;Derives plaintext passwords or valid hashes from target hash artifacts through computational attack methods.&lt;SEP&gt;The process attempts to crack captured password hashes into plaintext credentials.</data>
  <data key="d9">consumes,cracks,is processed by,produces,produces artifact from,results in,targets,tests or exploits,utilizes</data>
