<edge source="SQL Injection File Read" target="Arbitrary File Read">
  <data key="d7">15.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SQL Injection File Read is a cybersecurity attack technique that exploits vulnerabilities in SQL input handling to gain unauthorized access to arbitrary files stored on the server's filesystem. This method involves injecting malicious SQL queries that trick the application into performing actions beyond intended database operations, such as reading the contents of data files, configuration files, source code, encrypted credentials, or any sensitive resources residing on the server. Successful exploitation grants the attacker the capability to retrieve any file within the server's accessible storage, directly compromising data confidentiality and integrity by exposing secrets, authentication details, or other sensitive information. The ability to access such files indicates a severe breach, often aiding privilege escalation and further exploitation, while also allowing attackers to extract internal files containing authentication tokens, application logic, or other critical system assets necessary to expand their control over the compromised environment.</data>
  <data key="d9">can establish,can establish attacker capability,can support,enables,establishes,supports</data>
