  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The technique requires an available login workflow to authenticate and maintain session state during exploitation.&lt;SEP&gt;The presence of a legitimate login process or workflow provides a required input channel to inject queries targeting file retrieval.&lt;SEP&gt;The attack relies on a login endpoint to authenticate and maintain session context while injecting queries.&lt;SEP&gt;This technique requires a reachable login workflow to establish a valid query context to perform file reading.&lt;SEP&gt;Uses user-controlled input within a login-related query to obtain file system data.&lt;SEP&gt;When a functional login form or workflow is reachable and accepts input through SQL to extract or read data.</data>
