<edge source="SQL Injection File Read" target="User-Controlled Input Reaches Query">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SQL Injection File Read is a security vulnerability that occurs when unsanitized user-controlled input is directly incorporated into backend SQL queries without validation or escaping. This lack of input filtering allows attackers to inject malicious SQL statements into input fields, enabling the manipulation of query execution logic. Specifically, by injecting crafted SQL code into user inputs that reach query execution paths, an attacker can force the application to read sensitive internal files stored on the server, such as configuration files (e.g., web.config) or database dumps. The core requirement for this attack is successful delivery of the malicious input to an SQL query execution layer, bypassing security controls that would otherwise prevent unauthorized file read operations or execute unintended commands.</data>
  <data key="d9">applies when,enables,exploits,is applicable when,requires</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ce55c93390355c438aad3e42f2558ea0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da041acb6b82f70d6eea7e644d1ab933-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9756198566adacc24b429de0c91a0beb-chunk-000</data>
