<edge source="SSRF Localhost Probing" target="Localhost-Only Service Exists">
  <data key="d7">28.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The technique is applicable only when an internal service bound to localhost is exposed via an SSRF vector.&lt;SEP&gt;Localhost-Only Service Exists, SSRF Localhost Probing describes a security vulnerability condition wherein a service bound exclusively to the loopback address (either `127.0.0.1` in IPv4 or a specific IPv6 loopback address) becomes externally accessible. This relation represents the necessary precondition that enables Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) attacks. An attacker exploits this misconfiguration by injecting specially crafted URLs or request parameters into external inputs; the vulnerable application then interprets these as valid requests and issues outbound requests to the exposed loopback address. If the internal, localhost-bound service is reachable from the application due to this flaw, the attacker can retrieve sensitive internal data, bypass access controls, or perform further reconnaissance on the internal network infrastructure. The entire attack feasibility hinges on this very condition: the existence of an internal service bound to localhost that has been inadvertently exposed through the application's request handling mechanisms, making localhost injection a viable attack vector.&lt;SEP&gt;Probing techniques specifically target services reachable via localhost address.&lt;SEP&gt;Employs crafted URLs to probe or exploit a service bound to localhost.&lt;SEP&gt;This technique focuses on probing the existence or details of services that only respond to local IP addresses.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique requires a service restricted to localhost to probe and enumerate internal resources.&lt;SEP&gt;The attack is applicable only when a service bound to localhost can be reached via SSRF.&lt;SEP&gt;A locally accessible service can be targeted from within an application using SSRF to probe for trust boundaries.</data>
  <data key="d9">applicable when,applies when,detects through,enables,exploits,focuses on,is applicable when,relies on,requires,targets</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ccb6aa44b59c087ddbe71de229597bd4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-495dc2d2fa3a0bb201cd26ebaa77ad10-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a18d9206e0b44dc082a257441a96e79d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-39047a18b515fcf5a6bcfa50dda4ee3a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e758367fdb2b5f6f0ba25e5351f06fae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2af45459b5392b7945360d1fe34d952c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-66bd77b51f9ea38a4762d65732ac21c9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e4ab66012df8871bd0b67c09233a063-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-198b423c5fcf5fd72465af48d35436e5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff53209713af43febf0054a8036e08a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d193154c13a7545340d6aac7f93551ff-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d57f4dccb7b1de7c796c24d456b2c90f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4cbd3a65e3bbf220a047cbb226753147-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000</data>
