  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SSRF is possible when a service endpoint exists that performs server-side requests external to the host.&lt;SEP&gt;Uses API routes to send requests to the intentionally reachable loopback-based service.&lt;SEP&gt;SSRF probing abuses API endpoints that accept user-controlled input to reach localhost services.&lt;SEP&gt;Relies on accessible API endpoints to send requests to localhost or internal services.&lt;SEP&gt;The attacker leverages an exposed external service API that may blindly resolve or proxy requests back to local network.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique relies on sending requests to crafted URLs that the server internally resolves or forwards through APIs listening on internal interfaces.</data>
