<edge source="Weak Or Reused Password Exists" target="Offline Password Cracking">
  <data key="d7">21.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Offline Password Cracking via Weak or Reused Passwords is a cybersecurity threat whereby attackers exploit offline computational resources to validate and compromise password hashes when user credentials are either weak or previously exposed. The attack hinges on the condition that accounts utilize predictable, simple, or reused passwords; leveraging this weakness, malicious actors can employ brute-force, dictionary, or specialized offline cracking methods to derive valid access credentials from stored hash values. Once cracked, these credentials grant unauthorized access to the corresponding accounts. This technique is feasible only when captured hash lists contain weak or reused passwords, significantly elevating the risk of unauthorized access whenever stored user credentials fail to meet adequate complexity requirements or have been previously compromised via data breaches.&lt;SEP&gt;Capture or knowledge of weak credentials allows brute-force or dictionary attacks to succeed offline.&lt;SEP&gt;Requires that weak or reused passwords are present in captured credentials for successful cracking.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique requires weak or reused passwords to attempt decryption or verification of cracking efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;Exploits credential weaknesses such as easy-to-guess or reused passwords to reduce brute-force or dictionary cracking time.&lt;SEP&gt;Existence of weak passwords allows offline dictionary or brute-force attacks using obtained hash data.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique is relevant when password strength is insufficient or credentials have been reused from previous breaches.</data>
  <data key="d9">applicable when,applies when,depends on,enabled by,enables,implies,leverages,precondition for,relies on,requires,targets</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-dd80fa5ebb19e9944238770f478851fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d1d825cd69dea8aed6d1651fb993c0c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db51747d6e1553794dcbbc6d673eb1a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-39047a18b515fcf5a6bcfa50dda4ee3a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e60bdd5f7d1090f66c283ab2ebd04906-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b35a43e83892d75bc8e3746466c2bcfc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8047b6c93b09b89977542720f829a1da-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-28e61b57c4ef53155963a0bdc0146d46-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6ee3143291e5ed56b99323040f30f7d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a539186415b267cf2fe68e024581d476-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eff443bdc3f8249787b9d9ee690d679-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d9672c1c086c805dbb8f8962ec642b7a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-219fb4a2de2e4f86f2a836460b2e4201-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c76c270a0e4b9c50447afdcbfd22aa1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2af45459b5392b7945360d1fe34d952c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9756198566adacc24b429de0c91a0beb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3a8496df2ccf7a2fedc35b83bd6c5e51-chunk-002</data>
